Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250: make the crypto engine's DDR vote active-only

The QCE votes 393600 kBps on its path to DDR with tag 0, which icc-rpmh
treats as QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS, and the driver has no runtime PM: the
vote is taken at probe and never dropped. It goes into the RPMh sleep
set, so MC0 and SH0 stay voted through s2idle and DDR never enters
self-refresh (the APPS sleep set on a Retroid Pocket Flip 2 had MC0 and
SH0 non-zero; with the QCE unbound both went to 0).

The engine only moves data while a CPU drives it, so tag the path
QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY, like the CPU paths (0016).

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
@@ -2643,7 +2643,7 @@
 				 <&apps_smmu 0x59f 0x0000>,
 				 <&apps_smmu 0x586 0x0011>,
 				 <&apps_smmu 0x596 0x0011>;
-			interconnects = <&aggre2_noc MASTER_CRYPTO_CORE_0 0 &mc_virt SLAVE_EBI_CH0 0>;
+			interconnects = <&aggre2_noc MASTER_CRYPTO_CORE_0 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY &mc_virt SLAVE_EBI_CH0 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY>;
 			interconnect-names = "memory";
 		};
 
